                <pb facs="0625" n="619" sameAs="frus:frus1894app1/pg619"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Sir Julian Pauncefote
                        to Mr. Gresham.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1894-05-01"><hi rendition="#italic">May 1, 1894</hi></date>.
                        (Received May 2.)</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With reference to my note of the 14th
                    ultimo, respecting hostilities in Samoa, I have now the honor to inform you, in
                    accordance with instructions from the Earl of Kimberley, that Her Majesty’s
                    consul at Apia reported by telegraph on the 27th of March last that he has still
                    hopes that peace may be restored in Samoa, and that he does not share the
                    anxiety felt by his United States colleague.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Julian
                    Pauncefote.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
